WEBVTT

00:13.179 --> 00:15.098
<i>This is strange.</i>

00:16.474 --> 00:18.767
<i>Even though I'm facing death,</i>

00:18.768 --> 00:21.187
<i>I'm not scared in the slightest.</i>

00:24.524 --> 00:25.483
<i>That's right.</i>

00:26.317 --> 00:28.570
<i>It's because I'm not alone.</i>

00:30.405 --> 00:34.409
<i>I'm sure they will bring Stanley down...</i>

00:36.536 --> 00:37.454
<i>through the power</i>

00:38.288 --> 00:40.331
<i>of their science...</i>

00:43.918 --> 00:45.295
<i>Senku...</i>

00:48.173 --> 00:49.132
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

02:26.604 --> 02:28.772
Three thousand meters,

02:28.773 --> 02:31.276
one second!

02:33.903 --> 02:35.696
Amazeballs!

02:35.697 --> 02:37.781
The blast of the shock cannon...

02:37.782 --> 02:40.577
It even cracked the saucer!

02:41.619 --> 02:42.744
All we have to do

02:42.745 --> 02:45.080
is place the completed
petrification device here,

02:45.081 --> 02:46.457
and then we win.

02:47.333 --> 02:48.293
However...

02:51.796 --> 02:53.297
Not again!

02:53.298 --> 02:54.882
This is hell!

02:54.883 --> 02:57.844
They made sure to cut it
so it would crack easily.

02:58.469 --> 03:01.890
Damn! We don't have time for this!

03:08.771 --> 03:11.774
Please, Kohaku! Tsukasa! Hyoga!

03:12.817 --> 03:16.070
You've got to stop Stanley somehow.

03:20.825 --> 03:21.742
How about this?

03:21.743 --> 03:25.914
It will hold us up
until we fix the communication device.

03:29.000 --> 03:31.628
Negative. We are not halting.

03:32.337 --> 03:34.254
The three who attacked us earlier

03:34.255 --> 03:37.634
were the strongest members
of Senku's Science Club.

03:38.593 --> 03:41.220
This has definitely been
a dangerous reconnaissance mission,

03:41.221 --> 03:43.765
and he sent all his trump cards at once.

03:44.474 --> 03:46.934
It surely was an awkward move
on their part.

03:46.935 --> 03:49.896
There's a reason they tried to buy time,
even if it meant dying.

03:51.397 --> 03:53.274
I can smell it.

03:53.775 --> 03:56.068
My gut's telling me.

03:56.069 --> 03:57.278
I won't...

03:59.989 --> 04:01.532
let them attack!

04:02.283 --> 04:03.409
We'll ditch our comms,

04:03.993 --> 04:08.331
and annihilate the enemy's base at once!

04:13.127 --> 04:14.045
Luna.

04:15.338 --> 04:19.092
The resurrection is absolutely necessary
for our suicide petrification mission.

04:20.218 --> 04:22.512
Since Suika's group has been captured,

04:24.764 --> 04:26.014
you'll be their substitute.

04:26.015 --> 04:27.140
Huh?

04:27.141 --> 04:29.101
Sure! Leave it to me!

04:29.102 --> 04:31.311
I'm okay with it. I'm cool with it!

04:31.312 --> 04:33.273
But... why me?

04:35.149 --> 04:36.942
Should any stone statues get shattered

04:36.943 --> 04:40.028
or end up with missing pieces
or broken fingers,

04:40.029 --> 04:42.073
you could fix them as a doctor!

04:44.701 --> 04:46.786
We'll add Chelsea as a guide.

04:47.412 --> 04:49.080
You two, hide far away.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.750
Okay.

04:56.170 --> 04:57.796
Damn you, Carlos!

04:57.797 --> 05:01.174
Why let our lady go?
We could be her guards...

05:01.175 --> 05:03.636
We'll get going, then!

05:09.517 --> 05:11.978
When it comes to guidance,
you can count on me.

05:13.688 --> 05:17.316
I'll take you somewhere safe, Luna.

05:17.317 --> 05:19.319
No matter what...

05:30.496 --> 05:33.999
What's wrong? Are you okay?
Why, all of a sudden?

05:34.000 --> 05:35.709
I'm sorry!

05:35.710 --> 05:38.170
I'm suddenly acting weird!

05:38.171 --> 05:39.630
LOL.

05:51.517 --> 05:53.394
<i>Four hostages.</i>

05:54.187 --> 05:58.691
<i>No sign of Kohaku, Tsukasa, or Hyoga,
the ones who went to stop them.</i>

05:59.734 --> 06:01.444
<i>Which means...</i>

06:03.071 --> 06:06.657
Everyone... they all know it.

06:07.241 --> 06:10.161
The petrification device
won't be ready on time...

06:11.245 --> 06:15.792
<i>All they can do is keep trying
until time runs out.</i>

06:18.002 --> 06:21.255
That's why they asked
you and me to escape.

06:21.798 --> 06:24.175
We can't fight.

06:31.766 --> 06:34.434
- Senku! Carlos! Max!
- No! Stop!

06:34.435 --> 06:37.688
They're going to kill them!
I won't let that happen!

06:49.617 --> 06:51.785
No way!

06:51.786 --> 06:54.871
How did Stanley manage
to arrive this fast?

06:54.872 --> 06:56.540
Well!

06:56.541 --> 06:58.501
I'll stop them here!

06:59.085 --> 06:59.960
I'll hold them off

06:59.961 --> 07:03.673
until the science team
finishes the petrification device!

07:06.050 --> 07:08.553
I'll buy them at least a second!

07:12.765 --> 07:15.810
Let me make this crystal clear.

07:16.394 --> 07:20.480
The moment we break in,
shoot down everyone on sight except Xeno.

07:20.481 --> 07:21.816
Do not accept any surrenders.

07:23.734 --> 07:24.652
Roger that.

07:32.618 --> 07:33.953
Taiju!

07:42.712 --> 07:44.881
Hey, wake up, Taiju...

07:45.506 --> 07:46.841
You're kidding me, right?

07:48.134 --> 07:50.218
Aren't you invincible?

07:50.219 --> 07:52.388
Don't you always get back up?

07:53.306 --> 07:54.724
Taiju is...

08:03.065 --> 08:06.068
Science Kingdom vs Science Kingdom.

08:06.819 --> 08:09.070
It's about time for the ultimate showdown

08:09.071 --> 08:11.449
to decide who gets to rule Earth.

08:12.074 --> 08:16.244
Yes. Right now,
there isn't a single person on Earth

08:16.245 --> 08:19.040
who can take Stanley down, is there?

08:20.082 --> 08:22.417
We knew that we couldn't get Senku

08:22.418 --> 08:25.546
to work with us
on our plan to dominate the world.

08:26.631 --> 08:30.384
Our only options
were to kill him or imprison him for life.

08:31.385 --> 08:36.724
But if any of you were
to cooperate with us, then you'd...

08:38.684 --> 08:41.144
That isn't elegant of you, Xeno.

08:41.145 --> 08:43.606
Who said this is over?

08:44.732 --> 08:46.359
One second of grit is a step closer!

08:47.276 --> 08:49.237
<i>Two seconds of grit are two steps closer!</i>

08:50.196 --> 08:53.824
<i>Senku and his team will always
look toward the future of science.</i>

08:55.326 --> 08:57.203
Did you forget, Dr. Xeno?

08:57.745 --> 08:59.454
The essence of science

08:59.455 --> 09:04.585
is steadily driving a wedge
into the future, isn't it?

09:05.836 --> 09:08.089
No matter who falls along the way,

09:09.131 --> 09:11.884
we'll be the ones to win in the end.

09:13.302 --> 09:16.138
<i>Petrify everything, save everything.</i>

09:16.973 --> 09:20.434
<i>With the future of science, Dr. Stone!</i>

09:37.159 --> 09:39.369
No! No!

09:39.370 --> 09:42.290
No!

10:02.602 --> 10:04.979
All the diamonds burned...

10:09.066 --> 10:13.904
In the end, I couldn't do anything at all...

10:14.614 --> 10:20.494
<i>We all thought so hard
and put so much effort into it.</i>

10:21.621 --> 10:24.789
<i>But in the end, Medusa belongs to Whyman,</i>

10:24.790 --> 10:28.252
<i>and it's a planet we humans can't reach.</i>

10:28.836 --> 10:34.300
I couldn't even
take a single step into the future.

10:37.011 --> 10:38.804
Not even a single step?

10:39.347 --> 10:42.350
No, not necessarily...

10:42.892 --> 10:46.187
It's just that we couldn't do it
with our skills alone!

10:48.064 --> 10:49.190
Huh?

10:52.151 --> 10:53.402
A call?

10:54.195 --> 10:55.780
From who?

10:58.407 --> 10:59.659
Could it be...

11:00.242 --> 11:04.413
<i>from Corn City in North America?</i>

11:04.914 --> 11:08.250
<i>Is it our ace watchmaker, Joel?</i>

11:10.461 --> 11:12.921
0.03 meters,

11:12.922 --> 11:14.048
ten seconds.

11:15.508 --> 11:17.133
As a professional,

11:17.134 --> 11:19.929
I've decided that every time
I finish an important job,

11:20.638 --> 11:23.348
I'd drink this cup of victory
to the last drop,

11:23.349 --> 11:25.559
without any disruption.

11:27.770 --> 11:29.355
I found it.

11:30.564 --> 11:34.568
A piece of future science that didn't
even exist in the 21st century.

11:35.444 --> 11:38.154
For the eternity of humankind!

11:38.155 --> 11:40.950
PETRIFICATION DEVICE ACQUIRED!!

11:46.705 --> 11:49.499
From now on, as long as I've got time,

11:49.500 --> 11:53.211
I can grind out as many
diamond batteries as you need.

11:53.212 --> 11:56.715
Though maybe it's
only possible with my skills.

11:57.299 --> 11:59.384
<i>Kaseki, it's all thanks to you.</i>

11:59.385 --> 12:00.344
Huh?

12:11.647 --> 12:13.691
They're splitting in two?

12:14.692 --> 12:16.818
Maybe it's a coded message.

12:16.819 --> 12:18.319
Sounds fishy...

12:18.320 --> 12:21.906
As a precaution,
all suspicious communications from now on

12:21.907 --> 12:25.244
will be off-limits
to the Science Club kids.

12:26.162 --> 12:28.122
Morse code through a watch?

12:28.706 --> 12:31.208
So it's just a listening device?

12:31.709 --> 12:33.752
What do they mean by 'splitting in two'?

12:34.295 --> 12:36.254
That channel's only used
for technical info

12:36.255 --> 12:38.506
about diamond battery production.

12:38.507 --> 12:41.385
I don't think it was a pointless report.

12:41.886 --> 12:47.016
Maybe they're stuck
on how to cut the diamonds at the moment.

12:47.600 --> 12:50.144
Could it be that your Japanese team

12:50.728 --> 12:53.189
<i>has a professional engineer among you?</i>

12:54.106 --> 12:55.107
<i>Kaseki!</i>

12:58.777 --> 13:01.446
It split perfectly in two!

13:01.447 --> 13:03.656
Diamond batteries
have fragile cleavage planes,

13:03.657 --> 13:05.493
making them prone to cracking
in the middle.

13:06.076 --> 13:07.994
You helped a lot, Kaseki!

13:07.995 --> 13:13.542
Understanding that kind of logic
is a remarkable feat!

13:14.251 --> 13:16.377
Good, I'll grind out more.

13:16.378 --> 13:20.549
I'll stake my pride
as a professional jeweler and watchmaker!

13:22.176 --> 13:26.012
That's the lowdown, Kaseki.
It was glorious to witness

13:26.013 --> 13:28.307
the first artificial Medusa.

13:30.017 --> 13:33.103
This is our shared achievement.

13:34.647 --> 13:36.147
I'm so happy!

13:36.148 --> 13:39.735
My efforts weren't useless, after all.

13:40.236 --> 13:44.073
It's all I've worked on my entire life.

13:45.407 --> 13:46.908
It's strange.

13:46.909 --> 13:48.701
Even when I die,

13:48.702 --> 13:55.083
even when anyone dies,
science alone will surpass life itself

13:55.084 --> 13:58.337
and carry on into the future!

14:07.513 --> 14:10.223
Did you try it in a glass
so it wouldn't get confiscated

14:10.224 --> 14:12.226
right after you finished?

14:19.817 --> 14:21.610
<i>I'm sorry, that's not happening.</i>

14:22.570 --> 14:25.030
<i>I'm taking this right away.</i>

14:26.240 --> 14:28.409
<i>This would turn into a terrible weapon.</i>

14:41.714 --> 14:44.424
My only little regret is that

14:44.425 --> 14:48.220
I didn't get
to congratulate Joel in the end.

14:48.804 --> 14:51.055
Just say it over the radio!

14:51.056 --> 14:54.351
It doesn't matter
if Stanley and his crew hear it now.

14:55.811 --> 14:57.104
That's right.

14:57.688 --> 14:59.063
That's fine.

14:59.064 --> 15:03.235
There's a chance Stanley's team
has no communications at the moment.

15:04.820 --> 15:08.616
<i>Don't you think
those guys are being way too pushy?</i>

15:09.450 --> 15:11.826
<i>No final report over the comms,</i>

15:11.827 --> 15:13.703
<i>ignoring the white flag...</i>

15:13.704 --> 15:15.622
<i>Maybe the comms got destroyed</i>

15:15.623 --> 15:18.292
<i>and the hostage power balance
got messed up.</i>

15:19.126 --> 15:22.587
I mean, there's no way
Kohaku and the others

15:22.588 --> 15:26.008
would just stand there and do nothing!

15:26.592 --> 15:28.676
Yes, so now...

15:28.677 --> 15:32.139
we could be the ones
monopolizing communications!

15:32.973 --> 15:34.515
If that's the case...

15:34.516 --> 15:35.642
Yes...

15:35.643 --> 15:37.645
Our last one in a million chance!

15:49.281 --> 15:51.199
It's Japanese.

15:51.200 --> 15:53.534
Are they still talking about engineering?

15:53.535 --> 15:56.705
If you don't tell me the English,
I'll cut it mid-message.

16:19.520 --> 16:21.480
Oh, interesting...

16:22.189 --> 16:26.402
I'm getting tired of staying quiet
around other people!

16:28.487 --> 16:30.488
We should have all launched

16:30.489 --> 16:32.700
a suicidal frontal attack from the start!

16:33.200 --> 16:35.619
No, we would have been wiped out!

16:36.203 --> 16:37.036
Correct.

16:37.037 --> 16:39.163
Even if we all fall,

16:39.164 --> 16:41.791
science will continue
moving into the future,

16:41.792 --> 16:43.127
surpassing life itself!

16:51.802 --> 16:55.180
<i>Why is their faith so strong?</i>

16:55.681 --> 16:56.682
<i>What's their deal?</i>

16:57.975 --> 16:58.891
<i>Well...</i>

16:58.892 --> 17:03.439
<i>I guess I'll have to drink
my cup of victory too,</i>

17:04.940 --> 17:07.860
<i>with that engineer, Kaseki.</i>

17:13.365 --> 17:17.536
<i>From your place in North America
to ours in South America.</i>

17:18.037 --> 17:21.582
<i>We'll cover it all with Medusa!</i>

17:24.001 --> 17:25.753
<i>Everyone's been killed.</i>

17:26.378 --> 17:28.588
<i>This is our only chance of winning.</i>

17:28.589 --> 17:30.799
<i>Our first and only chance.</i>

17:33.969 --> 17:37.013
<i>The great disaster
that petrified the world</i>

17:37.014 --> 17:39.182
<i>3,700 years ago...</i>

17:39.183 --> 17:42.728
<i>we'll trigger it once again
with our own science!</i>

17:43.812 --> 17:47.566
We will destroy all of humanity...

17:48.192 --> 17:49.735
and then save them!

17:55.365 --> 17:56.783
<i>These freaks...</i>

17:56.784 --> 17:58.952
<i>They suddenly decided
to launch a suicide attack!</i>

17:59.495 --> 18:00.537
<i>But why?</i>

18:01.080 --> 18:02.497
Go!

18:02.498 --> 18:04.624
They're coming
for the petrification device!

18:04.625 --> 18:05.918
Don't let them touch it!

18:08.962 --> 18:10.379
It hurts!

18:10.380 --> 18:12.298
If we die, who knows...

18:12.299 --> 18:14.217
But if we don't, we'll be fine!

18:14.218 --> 18:16.220
Don't hesitate and go get them!

18:28.440 --> 18:29.483
Those are the keys!

19:34.965 --> 19:36.382
It's over.

19:36.383 --> 19:39.469
Yes, that was all of them.

19:45.684 --> 19:46.685
Huh?

20:01.658 --> 20:05.120
Don't let the petrification device
get near his mouth!

20:07.414 --> 20:10.125
Hey, what a pity, Joel.

20:10.626 --> 20:11.919
Why did you betray us?

20:12.711 --> 20:16.380
It's my revenge for my Bourbon...

20:16.381 --> 20:19.550
I wouldn't let anyone disrupt
my drink of victory,

20:19.551 --> 20:21.803
and you got in my way.

20:22.512 --> 20:23.931
That's all.

20:26.183 --> 20:27.976
What a pretentious thing to say.

20:28.560 --> 20:31.229
You just didn't want them all to die

20:31.230 --> 20:34.023
before talking to Kaseki
from the Science Club

20:34.024 --> 20:36.484
about Medusa's structure, right?

20:36.485 --> 20:38.819
Don't try to act all tough, kid.

20:38.820 --> 20:42.366
I'm an engineer, too. I know what you're...

20:44.660 --> 20:45.702
<i>That sound...</i>

20:47.788 --> 20:49.790
<i>A communicator disguised as a watch?</i>

20:50.999 --> 20:52.833
Don't let anyone near the radio!

20:52.834 --> 20:56.296
Someone might shout
and trigger the petrification device!

20:56.880 --> 20:58.631
"Someone"?

20:58.632 --> 21:00.926
But we brought them all down.

21:02.427 --> 21:05.471
We won't be the ones raising our voices.

21:05.472 --> 21:07.391
That's God's job.

21:08.850 --> 21:10.851
You don't know?

21:10.852 --> 21:14.564
It comes up a lot in science class.

21:16.108 --> 21:19.653
All the time, a massive radio wave scream

21:20.570 --> 21:25.075
flows continuously from heaven to Earth!

21:27.953 --> 21:33.750
<i>Twelve million 800 thousand meters,
one second.</i>

21:39.589 --> 21:41.842
I can't believe that in the end,

21:42.592 --> 21:44.010
it'll be Whyman...

21:44.011 --> 21:46.930
no, Senku's voice...

21:48.348 --> 21:50.350
that destroys the world

21:51.059 --> 21:52.936
and saves everyone.

22:08.201 --> 22:09.911
<i>With our future science,</i>

22:11.371 --> 22:13.123
<i>our Dr. Stone.</i>

23:53.431 --> 23:55.933
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.934 --> 23:57.810
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:57.811 --> 23:59.478
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM
MAY BE DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL,

23:59.479 --> 24:00.938
SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:00.939 --> 24:01.898
Subtitle translation by: Silvia Tomey
